.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt HDIUTIL 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm hdiutil
.Nd manipulate disk images
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm create
.Op Fl size Ar size
.Op Fl fs Ar filesystem
.Op Fl volname Ar name
.Op Fl layout Cm GPTSPUD | NONE
.Op Fl srcfolder Ar folder
.Op Fl format Ar format
.Op Fl imagekey Li zlib-level= Ns Ar n
.Op Fl ov
.Ar image
.Nm
.Cm convert
.Ar image
.Fl format Ar format
.Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl imagekey Li zlib-level= Ns Ar n
.Op Fl ov
.Nm
.Cm attach
.Op Fl readonly
.Op Fl nomount
.Op Fl mountpoint Ar path
.Ar image
.Nm
.Cm detach | eject
.Op Fl force
.Ar device | mountpoint
.Nm
.Cm info
.Nm
.Cm imageinfo
.Ar image
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
attaches disk images as disks through the kernel's MinkarDiskImage driver:
an image becomes
.Pa /dev/disk Ns Ar N ,
its partitions are published as on any disk, and their volumes are mounted
in
.Pa /Volumes
under their names.
It needs root.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm create
Make a raw image of
.Ar size
(with a
.Li b
(512-byte sectors),
.Li k , m , g
or
.Li t
suffix; or, with
.Fl srcfolder ,
large enough for the folder, whose contents are copied in).
The name gets
.Pa .dmg
unless it has an extension.
.Fl layout Cm GPTSPUD ,
the default, gives it a GUID partition table with one partition;
.Cm NONE ,
none.
.Fl fs
is
.Li HFS+
(the default),
.Li Journaled HFS+
or
.Li MS-DOS .
.Fl format
.Cm UDZO , UDBZ , ULFO
or
.Cm UDRO
makes it, then converts it (see
.Cm convert ) ;
with another format, or
.Fl type ,
the image is raw.
.It Cm convert
Write
.Ar image
(any image read here) as a new image,
.Ar output ,
in
.Ar format :
.Cm UDZO
(zlib; its level from
.Fl imagekey Li zlib-level= Ns Ar n ,
1 by default),
.Cm UDBZ
(bzip2),
.Cm ULFO
(LZFSE),
.Cm UDRO
(read-only, not compressed),
.Cm UDRW
(read/write) or
.Cm UDTO
(a raw master,
.Pa .cdr ) .
The disk is stored in 1 MB chunks; a chunk of zeros takes no room, and
one that saves less than an eighth is stored as it is.
The name gets
.Pa .dmg
.Pq Pa .cdr
unless it has an extension.
.It Cm attach
Attach an image and mount its volumes
.Pf ( Fl nomount :
none;
.Fl mountpoint :
the first at
.Ar path ) .
A read-only image file, a compressed or read-only UDIF image, or
.Fl readonly ,
attaches read-only.
Prints the disk and its partitions, with their content and mount points.
.It Cm detach , eject
Unmount the image's volumes (by force with
.Fl force )
and detach it.
.It Cm info
List the attached images.
.It Cm imageinfo
Show an image's format and size.
.El
.Pp
Raw images (what
.Cm create
makes, and CD/DVD masters) and UDIF images are read: read/write (UDRW),
read-only (UDRO) and compressed with ADC (UDCO), zlib (UDZO), bzip2
(UDBZ) or LZFSE (ULFO), the kernel decompressing a chunk when it is
read.
LZMA images (ULMO) are converted but not attached; segmented images are
not read.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstyp 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr newfs_hfs 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8
